%description:

Tcp.stopOperationTimeout:shorter -- the stop of TCP ends at the timeout, before the end of the extra time.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Timeout value for lifecycle stop operation".

The classes: longer (2s, the default: longer than the extra time, so the stage of TCP ends at
the end of the extra time) and shorter (shorter than stopOperationExtraTime: the stage ends at
the timeout). The code: Tcp::handleStopOperation() deletes all connections at once, then
delayActiveOperationFinish() schedules the timeout and startActiveOperationExtraTimeOrFinish()
the end of the extra time; OperationalMixin::handleMessage() ends the stage at the first of
the two, and at the timeout it calls handleCrashOperation() first. The stage of TCP waits for
no connection, so the timeout matters only when the extra time is longer (finding PF-10). This test separates "shorter" from the other class.

Host under test: host1, with an extra time of 1 s (precondition); host1 has no application. host2 sends a ping to host1 every 50 ms from 0.525 s on, so the
ping n leaves at 0.525 s + n * 50 ms. The tester stops host1 at 1.0 s with the lifecycle
operation of INET (stopNode). The stages of the stop go from the applications down: the
network layer of host1 goes down, and stops to answer pings, when the stage of TCP ends. Observation: level 1, the
last reply that host2 gets is the reply to the ping 19 (1.475 s): the stage of TCP ends at 1.5 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.stopOperationTimeout
%# class: shorter
%# value: 0.5s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.stopOperationTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpStopOperationTimeoutShorter")
        .once(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                  .filterValue(0)
                  .describe("the reply to the first ping")
                  .within(0.6))
        .act(action().at(1.0).stopNode("host1").describe("stop host1"))
        .once(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                  .filterValue(19)
                  .describe("the reply to the ping 19, sent at 1.475 s")
                  .within(0.485))
        .never(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                   .filterValueAtLeast(20)
                   .describe("a reply after the end of the stage of TCP")
                   .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpStopOperationTimeoutShorter compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.stopOperationTimeout = 0.5s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.stopOperationExtraTime = 1s
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host2.numApps = 1
*.host2.app[0].typename = "PingApp"
*.host2.app[0].destAddr = "host1"
*.host2.app[0].startTime = 0.525s
*.host2.app[0].sendInterval = 0.05s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpStopOperationTimeoutShorter: PASS
